  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Machado hit one for show. The offense. Ten strikeouts across six hits. Never made that matter.",
    "what_this_means": "This is a team that doesn't lead games anymore, just chases them. They trailed from the third inning forward, and even the bullpen's clean work. Matsui and Peralta combining for 3.2 scoreless innings. Couldn't bridge the gap an offense refused to close. The Dodgers broke it open in the fifth with three runs, and the Padres got one converted RISP chance but nothing else with runners in scoring position. Yuki Matsui and Jason Adam held together what was left, but a one-run RISP conversion across eight opportunities is not a recovery. This only works until the pitching can't hold anymore.",
    "what_to_watch": "Shota Imanaga brings a 4.40 ERA into tonight's matchup at Petco. The Padres need a clean start. Cubs are 2-3 at sea level this month. And their starter needs to match the bullpen's discipline.",
